;; Endeavor 149 rung 3 — staging with an OBSERVABLE SIDE EFFECT must NOT be replayed.
;;
;; NEGATIVE BY DESIGN, and it should stay negative forever.  Rungs 1 and 2 want replay to
;; start working; this one draws the line replay must not cross.
;;
;; THE HAZARD.  Replay re-runs the forward's staging statements at the top of the backward.
;; That is harmless when a statement only fills a LOCAL tile.  It is CORRUPTING when the same
;; statement also writes something observable — here `D`, a second &out parameter:
;;
;;     (set! (~ A-tile i) (~ A i))          ; pure fill        — safe to replay
;;     (set! (~ D i) (+ (~ D i) 1.0))       ; observable write — NOT safe to replay
;;
;; Replaying the block would increment D TWICE for one logical execution.  Nothing would
;; error; the kernel would simply produce a wrong D, in a build where the only thing that
;; changed is that AD was switched on.  That is the silent-wrong-answer class this project has
;; been bitten by repeatedly (135/01's plausible atomics returning 0.0; the fragment adjoint
;; that fell through a `when` and dropped the gradient without a word).
;;
;; THE CONTRACT.  When the statements the backward needs replayed are not provably free of
;; observable effects, the compiler REFUSES with a diagnostic naming the offending write.  It
;; does not replay-and-hope, and it does not silently skip the effectful statement either —
;; skipping would leave the tile half-filled and produce a wrong GRADIENT instead of a wrong D.
;;
;; A refusal is a fine outcome here.  The user can restructure (hoist the effect out of the
;; staging block) and get replay; what they must never get is a quiet double-write.
;;
;; NOTE ON THE EXPECTED MESSAGE.  The substring below is the CONTRACT this endeavour should
;; implement, chosen before the implementation exists — normal TDD.  If the eventual wording
;; differs, change the substring, but do not weaken what it asserts: the diagnostic must say
;; WHICH write made replay unsafe, or the user cannot act on it.
;;
;; COMPILE-WITH[--ir-target=spv]: PASS
;; COMPILE-WITH[--ir-target=spv --differentiate]: FAIL "side effect"
;; SKIP-DEFAULT-PASS

(def-type vec-t (vector float :address-space :global :align :compact))

(def-kernel staging_with_side_effect (A B &out C D)
  (declare #'(vec-t vec-t &out vec-t vec-t)
           (global-size :set-to 4)
           (local-size  :set-to 4))
  (let ((A-tile (make-scratch-vector float 4))
        (B-tile (make-scratch-vector float 4)))
    (workgroup-stride A-tile (i)
      (set! (~ A-tile i) (~ A i))
      (set! (~ B-tile i) (~ B i))
      ;; The observable write that makes this block unsafe to replay.
      (set! (~ D i) (+ (~ D i) 1.0)))
    (sync-workgroup)
    ;; The multiply is what would demand the primal, and therefore the replay.
    (workgroup-stride C (i)
      (set! (~ C i) (* (~ A-tile i) (~ B-tile i))))))
